WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.470 --> 00:01:14.470
Hey youtubers, this is going to be a breakdown
of the Episode 7 Trailer.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.729
Why is this trailer so special.

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:18.049
Because we knew so little about the film going
into it.

00:01:18.049 --> 00:01:20.150
This will not be the case with the other sequels.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.400
We’ll already know who most of the characters
are.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.690
The version they’re showing in theaters
is the same one.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.690
So everybody is seeing the same footage.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:27.890
First thing is the the voice over, I know
it sounds like Benedict Cumberbatch but I

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.100
think it’s Max Von Sydow.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.110
We only see a couple of the cast members,
but it’s all about new force sensitive characters

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.710
waking up to the force like Luke Skywalker
in Episode 4.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.420
Which is funny because John Boyega here looks
like he’s a stormtrooper on tatooine looking

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:52.770
for this soccer ball droid.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:59.730
The other side of this, the Dark Jedi at the
end with the modified lightsaber is also probably

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:03.190
one of the younger new cast members but I
don’t think we’ll find out who it is until

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.370
we get more footage.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:12.340
I’ve seen a few of the better rumors about
the arc of the film that I’ll mention at

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.930
the end of the video.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.280
But I don’t think this person is the one
doing the voice over.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.840
The modified John Williams Score.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.840
There are special trailers and then there
is this.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.800
Normally trailer music is taken from finished
cuts of the film or from general stock.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.159
Bringing Star Wars back is such a huge deal
they went one step further and had Williams

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:31.710
record special music just for the trailer.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:36.260
He’s scoring the entire film too, but the
trailer music is just a one off thing.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:55.430
Disney is probably going to make the audio
track available for download on iTunes eventually.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.830
Here’s a pretty awesome shot inside an imperial
troop transport.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.380
The Stormtrooper helmets look just like the
concept art from earlier this year.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:09.180
I think the reason they changed the look is
just to make them more practical.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.180
Just more streamlined.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.140
They even updated their blaster rifles here.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.850
Look how shiny.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:16.540
A lot of this I think is just to make it pop
on screen.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.910
The old ones were a dull black color.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:27.430
Of course they’re going to be selling these
toys in stores right as the movie comes out.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.650
This is Daisy Ridley, there are also a lot
of rumors about who she’s playing that I’ll

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.010
talk about in spoilers.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:38.390
The X-Wing’s we’ve already seen, they
along with the helmets and uniforms are also

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.920
slightly modified like the stormtroopers just
to pop on screen.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.959
The change in the design of the ships is probably
just to account for innovation in the 30 or

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.980
so year period since the original trilogy.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.301
I can’t tell which planet this is specifically
but they spent a lot of time on the movie

00:03:51.301 --> 00:03:55.489
filming on a lake that was doubling as a very
famous planet we haven’t seen in the movies

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:56.489
yet.

00:03:56.489 --> 00:03:58.480
If “It’s a Trap” rings any bells.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:05.300
But if this clears any questions about the
Empire and the Rebellion up, they’re both

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.300
relatively intact.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:11.239
I don’t know how they’re going to explain
the aftermath of the Battle of Yavin, but

00:04:11.239 --> 00:04:15.769
it seems like in this timeline, that was not
the huge blow to the empire that it was in

00:04:15.769 --> 00:04:17.350
the expanded universe.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:20.810
The period after that when the Thrawn Novels
picked up was kind of the begining of the

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:22.440
New Republic Era.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.810
And there won’t be a new republic in the
new trilogy.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.770
It will still be the Empire versus the Rebellion.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:34.300
We don’t know which planet this is but really
the lightsaber is what we should talk about.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:39.410
The new Rebels cartoon series intro’d another
highly modified lightsaber with the Inquisitor.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.840
Since Episode 7 is something of a beginning
for new force sensitive characters, I don’t

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.750
think we’ll be seeing a ton of dark jedi.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.880
Darth Maul had the double hilt.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.880
So this just looks like the latest Sith affectation.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.460
I think it’s interesting, it definitely
invokes imagery of a traditional broadsword.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.750
And they’ve updated the CG on the energy
blade effects to make them look almost like

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.860
trails of fire spitting out.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.780
That’s actually what drew my attention the
most.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.910
It’s makes the lightsaber seem like a much
more violent weapon.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.430
Less like a big glow stick.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:16.140
Millenium Falcon of course, looking badass
as always.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.270
Notice that they’ve finally repaired the
deflector dish.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.270
The new one isn’t circular.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.389
But the ship, just like the X-Wings is flying
around in the atmosphere of a planet.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.270
It think there’s a couple reasons they included
this shot.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:30.550
One is because it looks cool against the blue
sky background, but two.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:38.290
In the classic movies, space battles aren’t
super accurate with the way ships flying around

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.290
and fight each other.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.320
Battlestar Galactica, the Ronald D Moore reboot
series tried to do accurate space battles

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.830
with the ships manouvering like they actually
would, turning on a dime at really high speeds.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.190
I’m not a physicist, but it’s just things
in space wouldn’t have to turn in big circles

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.250
like ships in orbit.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:53.690
And that looks way cooler, so that’s why
I think they did this in the atmosphere of

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.690
a tatooine.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:55.720
Plus they can add these air trails.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:56.720
It’s scientifically more accurate and it
looks cooler.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.900
The tie fighters it’s fighting look relatively
the same.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.000
And all the sound effects also sound the same.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.820
If you’ve been watching the new rebels series,
they use all the classic sound foley.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.770
I’m sure they re-recorded a lot of them
over the years but for the most part they’re

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.070
all the original sounds.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:15.460
They’ll probably be showing off the first
full trailer at Celebration next year as a

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.040
convention exclusive and then releasing it
online.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.570
I know everyone wants something special for
star wars day on May 4th too.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:26.240
That’s right around the release of Avengers
2, so Disney will probably take advantage

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.680
of that.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.991
Overall the big takeaway is the tactile look
of the universe.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.770
JJ Abrams made it a big deal to do as much
real creature and practical effects as possible.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.320
Don’t be fooled though, there will still
be a shitload of CG.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:43.440
But because it’s so good now, they can use
CG to make everything look as dirty, lived-in

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:55.550
and steampunky 

00:06:55.550 --> 00:07:07.130
as 

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.789
the original trilogy.

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:29.530
One of the earliest comments I heard about
the prequels way way back was how clean everything

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:30.530
looked.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:08:05.030
So the visual style of this 

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:29.500
film is just a callback to the look of 
episode 4 5 and 6.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:51.190
I don’t expect to get 

00:08:51.190 --> 00:09:12.920
any official information about the characters
until Celebration, but that’s only a couple

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:13.920
months away.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:20.839
Disney is keeping as much of the details about
this as close to the vest as possible.

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:33.639
Which I totally don’t mind.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:57.600
For the first time in forever, we’re going
into a new Star Wars trilogy knowing almost

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:10.480
nothing about the story and the characters.

